A||||12||Yellow88GT||Stupid car show question.||||1||
Z||000000||Yellow88GT||06-13-2001||07:45 AM||||I'm going to take my GT to the Frankenmuth show in Michigan this year. <BR>This will be my first show.<P>My question is, what category do I enter my car in?<P>It is basically a stock GT with 17" rims.<BR>Oh yeah, it's also Yellow. <P>So does that make it modified, or custom, or can I still enter it<BR>into the stock GT category? (ok, that's 2 questions :-)<P>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/yellow88gt.JPG">  <P>I am not serious about competing, the car needs a lot of<BR>work to get to "show quality". I just want to make sure I<BR>am in the appropriate class.<P>Thanks,<P>Jerry<BR><p>[This message has been edited by Yellow88GT (edited 06-13-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000001||1FST2M6||06-13-2001||08:05 AM||||enter it in street 4x4.. LOL.. sorry.. uum what mods other then paint and wheels? any interior changes.. with just what you mentioned.. Street mild or what ever theat catagorey is just out of the stock class... <P>you need to hook up with Brent (Tigger) you two would make sweet pics orange and yellow... mmmm<P><BR>I've got the "Frankenmuth christmas bears" with the year on them since 77! (Lived in Port Huron for 15years and 3 in Sarnia, Ont)<P>welcome to the forum! <P>------------------<BR>       <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/sig1fst.jpg">       <BR>www.engineered.net<BR>www.enthuza.com||||reg||1
Z||000002||Yellow88GT||06-13-2001||08:26 AM||||Thanks 1FST2M6, the only interior mods are<BR>aftermarket pedals (also yellow) and some<BR>carbon fiber film installed over the console sections. <P>So I am starting to think that the stock<BR>class is out of the question at this point.<P>So the only other classes I could enter are:<P>___  Work in progress<BR>___  Custom<BR>___  Modified<P>I don't have enough miles on the car to get<BR>it into the Daily Driver Catagory.<P>Would modified be the best fit? <P>Jerry<P>||||reg||1
Z||000003||Indiana_resto_guy||06-13-2001||08:41 AM||||I would go with 'work in progress' if your doing improvements for better quality. (as in resto in progress)<BR>Why go with modified? Just for the wheels?||||reg||1
Z||000004||fierofreek2001||06-13-2001||11:10 AM||||how about daily driver class?    not sure if that show will have it or not..||||reg||1
Z||000005||RDosdorian||06-13-2001||11:32 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Yellow88GT:<BR><B>Thanks 1FST2M6, the only interior mods are<BR>aftermarket pedals (also yellow) and some<BR>carbon fiber film installed over the console sections. <P>So I am starting to think that the stock<BR>class is out of the question at this point.<P>So the only other classes I could enter are:<P>___  Work in progress<BR>___  Custom<BR>___  Modified<P>I don't have enough miles on the car to get<BR>it into the Daily Driver Catagory.<P>Would modified be the best fit? <P>Jerry<P></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>In most of the shows I have been involved with, the difference between “custom” and “modified” is this:<P>Custom – Exterior and Interior modifications.<P>Modified – Engine Conversions.<P>There is more to it, but if you do not have an engine conversion, you do not want to enter in the Modified Class.  This is only my opinion.  Others may disagree and that’s ok.  However, in most shows, the custom class tends to be a very large and competitive class.  Unfortunately for you, the minute you added the aftermarket wheels, you took yourself out of the stock class.  The other unfortunate thing is, (…and I am in the same boat with my 87 GT) wheels, pedals, and carbon fiber are not enough to make a car competitive in the custom class.<P>My suggestion to you and anybody else is…  Enter the show, have fun, talk Fieros, and don’t worry about winning an award.  All the award tells you is that a small group of individuals think your car is nice enough to earn an award.  What really matters is that you like your car (which looks great by the pic you posted) and that you are happy with your car.  Who really cares what other people think.<BR><P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.goldengatefieros.org/RDosdorian_sig.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000006||turbo86se||06-13-2001||12:27 PM||||Too bad Carlisle didn't have a work-in-progress section. I'd be all over that with my '88 coupe. I was in modified because of my V6 conversion. I was parked next to that sweet white/yellow V8 Fiero. The only comments I overheard about my Fiero is "why is this in modified?", or "T-Tops", and "why doesn't he do anything with the interior?" I was there just to have fun, put some serious miles on my freshly converted coupe, and meet some great people, which I did. <P>But then again, at Williamsburg last year there were Fieros in the modified class with custom wheels, and seat covers. Meanwhile I'm sitting there with my 86SE with a Miller Woods turbo system on mine. I guess it depends on the show. I also think shows should have a "black Fiero" class.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>At any rate, you've got a sweet Fiero, go there and show it off!!<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/View?u=226077&a=1676320&p=20236791"> ||||reg||7
Z||000007||Ditz88GT||06-13-2001||03:18 PM||||While we are on the subject of stupid car show questions I have one.  Where do some of these owners get those nice blankets to park there cars on.  I really think it helps the presentation, I just wondered where you would buy something like that.<P>~Ditz88GT<BR> <A HREF="http://go.to/fiero" TARGET=_blank>http://go.to/fiero</A> ||||reg||1
Z||000008||ferg||06-13-2001||03:37 PM||||I'd say work in progress.<P>I'm thinking of going, but I need to find out if the 5 hour drive will be worth it. How many cars typically attend? Is there a good swap meet with vendors?||||reg||1
Z||000009||Tigger||06-14-2001||08:40 AM||||Why not enter stock GT class?  Do you still have your stock wheels?  Fortunately, they just bolt on.    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P>BTW, Sweet looking GT!  Hope to see you at the show.<P>Brent<p>[This message has been edited by Tigger (edited 06-14-2001).]||||reg||3
Z||000010||Phil||06-14-2001||10:10 AM||||I assume you are talking about shows without a Fiero class. I would suggest that you stay out of modified( modified is almost like an unlimited class- anything goes). Generally custom is modifications other than drivetrain. I enter modified most of the time just to try to and give the Fiero some exposure. Very rarely do I even come close to  placing, for most car show people don't consider Fiero's "real" cars. No matter what class you're in you will be hard pressed to beat any GTO, Nova, Camaro or the like. But don't get discouraged. If you want a trophy go buy one, go to shows to have fun. <P>------------------<BR> <BR>      <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/88formula_1.gif">  <BR>SC 3800||||reg||1
Z||000011||Yellow88GT||06-14-2001||07:01 PM||||Thanks for all the replies'. I really appreciate it.<P>Indiana_resto_guy: Work in progress was the one I was leaning towards, but unfortunately my car is not tore up in a restoration. At least not yet  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>fierofreek2001: Unfortunately I don't have enough miles for it.<P>RDosdorian: Not what I wanted to hear  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif"> But most likely where I will end up entering it.<BR>Thanks for the info.<P>Turbo86se: Thanks, I will  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>Ditz88GT: Dunno  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>ferg: I think it is well attended, I don't know the numbers though. 50+ ?<P>Tigger: I wish. Unfortunately I sold my old rims to help pay for the Enkei's  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif"><BR>And thanks, look forward to meeting you.<P>Phil: The Michigan show I was talking about is the Michigan Fiero Fest. Nothing but <BR>Fieros  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">. I wouldn't want to go to any other kind  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>I really want to go, to see the other Fieros, and meet everybody at the show.<BR>I've read the other threads about other shows, and it sounds like a blast <P>Thanks again, <P>Jerry||||reg||1
Z||000012||FieroMaster88||06-14-2001||11:35 PM||||Wow, nice to see another michigan fiero owner!!!!  I am gonna say you will have to enter the custom class.  I had to at the carlisle show because i had a side scoop and pillar gauges!  DOH, it sucks. <P>You have a very nice car.  I hope to see you at the show.<P>------------------<BR>        <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/FieroMaster88.gif">        <BR>James Essar<BR>AOL IM Name: FieroMaster88<BR>88 Coupe 30,000 miles  <IMG SRC="http://cwm.ragesofsanity.com/s/net4/smiling2.gif"> ||||reg||1
